body:
@allenwp fair point. I do agree that sum/3 greyscale is suboptimal, I proposed it not because it's the best but because it was intended to be a simple addition to what we already had. What about using the weighted average of `0.299R + 0.587G + 0.114B` e.g.? I mean, there are always edge cases that are possible, and "greyscale" is an umbrella term that can mean different things based on context (e.g. sum/3 greyscale, while not the best, is still used in the wild where simplicity and speed is needed, and arguably it produces one of the "greyscales").

But you've also got a very good point with `max` - maybe we could add "Max RGB" (as you stated) and "Luminance" (with the weighted formula from above) to the remap options then?

My personal take is to allow as many options as reasonably possible, and to allow the game devs to experiment with them as needed, using the one that works best for them and their particular imported image. The heavy lifting is already done, writing one or two additional remapping functions won't cause any issues I think :)
